<title>GERMANY: One person hurt in German chemical plant accident.</title>
<headline>One person hurt in German chemical plant accident.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>One man was injured, suffering severe burns to his arms and neck, after an oil leak at Hoechst AG on Friday, the company said.</p>
<p>Hoechst AG, Germany's largest chemicals group, said the accident occurred at its Cassella plant in suburban Frankfurt when some 300 litres of a heat transmitting oil leaked.</p>
<p>A cloud of smoke wafted over the plant and police asked nearby residents to keep doors and windows shut, but Hoechst said the accident posed no threat to the public.</p>
</text>
